.cxx/
# Signing material. debug.keystore is the standard React Native debug key with
# the public password "android" — every RN app ships the same one, and it can
# sign nothing that matters. Everything else here is real: a release keystore,
# an App Store Connect API key, a provisioning profile. The release pipeline
# takes all of these from CI secrets, never from the repository.
*.keystore
!debug.keystore
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
play-service-account*.json
.kotlin/

# node.js
#
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# fastlane
#
# It is recommended to not store the screenshots in the git repo. Instead, use fastlane to re-generate the
# screenshots whenever they are needed.
# For more information about the recommended setup visit:
# https://docs.fastlane.tools/best-practices/source-control/

**/fastlane/report.xml
**/fastlane/Preview.html
**/fastlane/screenshots
**/fastlane/test_output

